# 必考词 Unit15
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit15核心词汇

{{eager}}{{/ˈiːɡər}}{{adj. 渴望的；热切的；热心的；急切的}}{{She is eager to learn new things.}}
{{earnest}}{{/ˈɜːnɪst}}{{adj. 认真的；诚挚的；郑重的；热心的}}{{He made an earnest effort to improve his grades.}}
{{eccentric}}{{/ɪkˈsentrɪk}}{{adj./n. 古怪的；怪人；异常的；不同圆心的}}{{The professor is known for his eccentric behavior.}}
{{eclipse}}{{/ɪˈklɪps}}{{n./v. 日食；月食；使黯然失色； eclipsing； ecliptic}}{{Her achievement eclipsed all previous records.}}
{{ecology}}{{/iˈkɒlədʒi}}{{n. 生态学；生态；社会生态学； ecological；生态环境}}{{The study of ecology is essential for understanding the environment.}}
{{economic}}{{/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪk}}{{adj. 经济的；经济学的；有利可图的；节约的；合算的}}{{The country is experiencing an economic boom.}}
{{economy}}{{/iˈkɒnəmi}}{{n. 经济；节约；经济体；经济制度；节省措施}}{{The global economy is showing signs of recovery.}}
{{edit}}{{/ˈedɪt}}{{v. 编辑；校订；剪辑；主编；编纂}}{{She edited the article before submission.}}
{{elaborate}}{{/ɪˈlæbərət}}{{adj./v. 精心制作的；详细阐述；复杂的；详尽的；精心的}}{{Could you elaborate on your proposal?}}
{{elapse}}{{/ɪˈlæps}}{{v. 时间流逝；过去；消逝；经过； elapsed}}{{Three hours elapsed before the meeting ended.}}
{{elect}}{{/ɪˈlekt}}{{v. 选举；选择；决定； elected；当选的}}{{The citizens elected a new president.}}
{{elegant}}{{/ˈelɪɡənt}}{{adj. 优雅的；精美的；简练的；讲究的；雅致的}}{{She wore an elegant dress to the dinner party.}}
{{element}}{{/ˈelɪmənt}}{{n. 元素；成分；要素；自然环境；基本原理}}{{Water is composed of two elements: hydrogen and oxygen.}}
{{elevate}}{{/ˈelɪveɪt}}{{v. 提升；举起；使高尚；提高；晋升}}{{The new policy aims to elevate the quality of education.}}
{{eligible}}{{/ˈelɪdʒəbl}}{{adj. 有资格的；合格的；合适的；符合条件的；具备条件的}}{{Only citizens over 18 are eligible to vote.}}
{{eliminate}}{{/ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt}}{{v. 消除；淘汰；排除；消灭；除去}}{{We must eliminate all errors before publication.}}
{{elite}}{{/eɪˈliːt}}{{n./adj. 精英；精英的；精华的；精锐的；出类拔萃的}}{{The university attracts elite students from around the world.}}
{{eloquent}}{{/ˈeləkwənt}}{{adj. 雄辩的；有口才的；富有表现力的；有说服力的；明白显示出的}}{{She is an eloquent speaker who captivates her audience.}}
{{embrace}}{{/ɪmˈbreɪs}}{{v./n. 拥抱；接受；包含；欣然接受；包围}}{{The company embraced new technology to improve productivity.}}
{{emerge}}{{/ɪˈmɜːdʒ}}{{v. 出现；浮现；显露；暴露；兴起}}{{New evidence emerged during the investigation.}}
{{emergency}}{{/ɪˈmɜːdʒənsi}}{{n. 紧急情况；突发事件；非常时刻；紧急状态}}{{In case of emergency, call 120 immediately.}}
{{emit}}{{/ɪˈmɪt}}{{v. 发出；排放；放射；发表；发行}}{{The factory emits large amounts of carbon dioxide.}}
{{emotion}}{{/ɪˈməʊʃn}}{{n. 情感；情绪；感动；激动；感情}}{{She tried to hide her emotions during the meeting.}}
{{emphasis}}{{/ˈemfəsɪs}}{{n. 强调；重点；重要性；加重语气；突出}}{{The teacher placed emphasis on critical thinking.}}
{{empirical}}{{/ɪmˈpɪrɪkl}}{{adj. 经验主义的；以实验为根据的；来自经验的；经验的；观察的}}{{The theory is supported by empirical evidence.}}
{{enable}}{{/ɪˈneɪbl}}{{v. 使能够；使可能；使可行；授予权利；使实现}}{{Technology enables us to communicate across the globe.}}
{{encounter}}{{/ɪnˈkaʊntər}}{{v./n. 遇到；遭遇；邂逅；冲突；交锋}}{{We encountered many difficulties during the trip.}}
{{encourage}}{{/ɪnˈkʌrɪdʒ}}{{v. 鼓励；促进；激励；助长；支持}}{{Teachers should encourage students to ask questions.}}
{{endow}}{{/ɪnˈdaʊ}}{{v. 赋予；捐赠；资助； endowed；天生具有}}{{She is endowed with great musical talent.}}
{{endure}}{{/ɪnˈdjʊər}}{{v. 忍受；持续；持久；忍耐；坚持}}{{She endured years of hardship before achieving success.}}
{{enforce}}{{/ɪnˈfɔːs}}{{v. 执行；强制；实施；迫使；强迫服从}}{{The police enforce the law to maintain order.}}
{{engage}}{{/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒ}}{{v. 从事；吸引；订婚；参与；占用}}{{She is engaged in scientific research.}}
{{enhance}}{{/ɪnˈhɑːns}}{{v. 提高；增强；改善；提升；美化}}{{Exercise enhances both physical and mental health.}}
{{enormous}}{{/ɪˈnɔːməs}}{{adj. 巨大的；庞大的；极大的；广大的；凶暴的}}{{The project requires an enormous amount of investment.}}
{{enrich}}{{/ɪnˈrɪtʃ}}{{v. 充实；使富裕；使丰富；使肥沃；浓缩}}{{Travel can enrich your life experience.}}
{{ensure}}{{/ɪnˈʃʊər}}{{v. 确保；保证；担保；保护；使安全}}{{Please ensure that all doors are locked before leaving.}}
{{enterprise}}{{/ˈentəpraɪz}}{{n. 企业；事业；进取心；冒险精神；事业心}}{{The enterprise has grown into a multinational corporation.}}
{{enthusiasm}}{{/ɪnˈθjuːziæzəm}}{{n. 热情；热心；热忱；积极性；激发热情的事物}}{{He showed great enthusiasm for the project.}}
{{entire}}{{/ɪnˈtaɪər}}{{adj. 整个的；全部的；完整的；完全的；全面的}}{{The entire family gathered for the holiday celebration.}}
{{entitle}}{{/ɪnˈtaɪtl}}{{v. 给予权利；给…命名；使有资格；给予；题名为}}{{This ticket entitles you to a free meal.}}
{{entity}}{{/ˈentəti}}{{n. 实体；存在；本质；实际存在物；独立存在体}}{{The company is a separate legal entity.}}
{{environment}}{{/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt}}{{n. 环境；自然环境；周围状况；工作环境；生态环境}}{{Protecting the environment is everyone's responsibility.}}
{{epidemic}}{{/ˌepɪˈdemɪk}}{{n./adj. 流行病；流行性的；蔓延的；极为盛行的}}{{The flu epidemic spread rapidly across the country.}}
{{episode}}{{/ˈepɪsəʊd}}{{n. 一集；插曲；事件；片段；一段经历}}{{The final episode of the series attracted millions of viewers.}}
{{epoch}}{{/ˈiːpɒk}}{{n. 时代；纪元；新纪元；时期；世}}{{The invention of the internet marked a new epoch in communication.}}
{{equality}}{{/iˈkwɒləti}}{{n. 平等；相等；均等；等式；等同性}}{{The fight for gender equality continues worldwide.}}
{{equivalent}}{{/ɪˈkwɪvələnt}}{{adj./n. 等同的；等价物；对等的人或物；相当的；等值的}}{{One mile is equivalent to 1.6 kilometers.}}
{{era}}{{/ˈɪərə}}{{n. 时代；纪元；年代；历史时期；阶段}}{{We are living in the era of digital transformation.}}
{{erode}}{{/ɪˈrəʊd}}{{v. 侵蚀；腐蚀；削弱；逐渐毁坏；风化}}{{The cliff has been eroded by the sea over centuries.}}
{{error}}{{/ˈerər}}{{n. 错误；过失；误差；谬误；罪过}}{{There was an error in the calculation.}}
{{erupt}}{{/ɪˈrʌpt}}{{v. 爆发；喷出；突然发生；出疹；喷发}}{{The volcano erupted violently last year.}}
{{escape}}{{/ɪˈskeɪp}}{{v./n. 逃跑；逃避；避开；泄漏；出口}}{{The prisoners attempted to escape from jail.}}
{{essence}}{{/ˈesns}}{{n. 本质；精华；精髓；香精；要素}}{{The essence of the argument is simple.}}
{{essential}}{{/ɪˈsenʃl}}{{adj. 必要的；本质的；基本的；必不可少的；根本的}}{{Water is essential for human survival.}}
{{establish}}{{/ɪˈstæblɪsh}}{{v. 建立；确立；创办；设立；证实}}{{The university was established in 1905.}}
{{estate}}{{/ɪˈsteɪt}}{{n. 房地产；财产；庄园；遗产； estate agent}}{{He invested in real estate and made a fortune.}}
{{estimate}}{{/ˈestɪmeɪt}}{{v./n. 估计；评价；估算；预算；判断}}{{The cost is estimated at two million dollars.}}
{{ethical}}{{/ˈeθɪkl}}{{adj. 伦理的；道德的；合乎道德的；伦理学的；道德准则的}}{{The company faces ethical questions about its practices.}}
{{evaluate}}{{/ɪˈvæljueɪt}}{{v. 评估；评价；求值；估计；鉴定}}{{The committee will evaluate all the applications.}}
{{eventually}}{{/ɪˈventʃuəli}}{{adv. 最终；终于；最后；终究；结果}}{{After years of hard work, she eventually achieved her goal.}}
{{evidence}}{{/ˈevɪdəns}}{{n. 证据；迹象；根据；证明；证词}}{{There is strong evidence to support the theory.}}
{{evoke}}{{/ɪˈvəʊk}}{{v. 唤起；引起；使人想起； evoke； evoke}}{{The song evoked memories of her childhood.}}
{{evolution}}{{/ˌiːvəˈluːʃn}}{{n. 进化；发展；演变；进化论；展开}}{{The theory of evolution was proposed by Darwin.}}
{{evolve}}{{/ɪˈvɒlv}}{{v. 进化；发展；逐步形成；展开；使发展}}{{Languages evolve over time.}}
{{exaggerate}}{{/ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt}}{{v. 夸张；夸大；言过其实； exaggerating；夸张的}}{{He tends to exaggerate his achievements.}}
{{exceed}}{{/ɪkˈsiːd}}{{v. 超过；超越；胜过；越出；优于}}{{Sales exceeded expectations this quarter.}}
{{exceptional}}{{/ɪkˈsepʃənl}}{{adj. 异常的；杰出的；例外的；特殊的；卓越的}}{{She has exceptional talent in music.}}
{{excerpt}}{{/ˈeksɜːpt}}{{n./v. 摘录；节选；引用；选取；选段}}{{The teacher read an excerpt from the novel.}}
{{excess}}{{/ɪkˈses}}{{n./adj. 过量；过量的；过多的；超额的；过度的}}{{An excess of sugar is bad for your teeth.}}
{{exclude}}{{/ɪkˈskluːd}}{{v. 排除；排斥；拒绝接纳；驱逐；不包括}}{{The price excludes tax and delivery charges.}}
{{exclusive}}{{/ɪkˈskluːsɪv}}{{adj. 排他的；独家的；高级的；专有的；奢华的}}{{The club is exclusive to members only.}}
{{execute}}{{/ˈeksɪkjuːt}}{{v. 执行；处决；实施；完成；演奏}}{{The plan was executed perfectly.}}
{{exemplify}}{{/ɪɡˈzemplɪfaɪ}}{{v. 举例说明；作为…的例证；例示；示范}}{{This case exemplifies the problem we are facing.}}
{{exempt}}{{/ɪɡˈzempt}}{{v./adj. 免除；被免除的；豁免的；免税的}}{{Students with high grades are exempt from the final exam.}}
{{exert}}{{/ɪɡˈzɜːt}}{{v. 施加；运用；发挥； exert oneself；努力}}{{She exerted great influence on the decision.}}
{{exhaust}}{{/ɪɡˈzɔːst}}{{v./n. 使筋疲力尽；废气；排气装置；用尽；耗尽}}{{The long hike exhausted everyone.}}
{{exhibit}}{{/ɪɡˈzɪbɪt}}{{v./n. 展示；展览品；陈列；表现；显示}}{{The museum exhibits rare paintings from the 18th century.}}
{{expand}}{{/ɪkˈspænd}}{{v. 扩大；膨胀；扩展；展开；详述}}{{The company plans to expand into Asian markets.}}
{{explicit}}{{/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt}}{{adj. 明确的；清楚的；直言的；详述的；显然的}}{{The instructions must be explicit and easy to follow.}}
{{exploit}}{{/ɪkˈsplɔɪt}}{{v./n. 开发；利用；功绩； exploitation；剥削}}{{We should exploit renewable energy resources.}}
{{explore}}{{/ɪkˈsplɔːr}}{{v. 探索；考察；勘探；研究；探险}}{{They explored the ancient ruins in the jungle.}}
{{expose}}{{/ɪkˈspəʊz}}{{v. 暴露；揭露；使曝光；显示；使遭受}}{{The report exposed corruption in the government.}}
{{extensive}}{{/ɪkˈstensɪv}}{{adj. 广泛的；大量的；广阔的；全面的；广博的}}{{The library has an extensive collection of books.}}
{{extent}}{{/ɪkˈstent}}{{n. 程度；范围；广度；长度；区域}}{{To what extent do you agree with this statement?}}
{{external}}{{/ɪkˈstɜːnl}}{{adj. 外部的；外面的；外界的；表面的；外用的}}{{The external walls of the building need repainting.}}
{{extract}}{{/ɪkˈstrækt}}{{v./n. 提取；摘录；榨取；选取；精华}}{{They extracted oil from the ground.}}
{{extraordinary}}{{/ɪkˈstrɔːdnri}}{{adj. 非凡的；特别的；异常的；卓越的；非凡的}}{{She has extraordinary talent in music.}}
{{extreme}}{{/ɪkˈstriːm}}{{adj./n. 极端的；极度；末端的；偏激的；极端行为}}{{Extreme weather events are becoming more frequent.}}
{{fabricate}}{{/ˈfæbrɪkeɪt}}{{v. 捏造；制造；建造；伪造；装配}}{{He fabricated evidence to support his claim.}}
{{facilitate}}{{/fəˈsɪlɪteɪt}}{{v. 促进；使便利；推动；帮助；使容易}}{{Technology facilitates communication between people.}}
{{factor}}{{/ˈfæktər}}{{n. 因素；因子；要素；系数；代理人}}{{Several factors contributed to the success of the project.}}
{{fade}}{{/feɪd}}{{v. 褪色；消退；凋谢；逐渐消失；衰弱}}{{The color of the curtain has faded over the years.}}
{{faith}}{{/feɪθ}}{{n. 信念；信仰；信任；忠诚；宗教信仰}}{{She has great faith in her children's abilities.}}
{{famine}}{{/ˈfæmɪn}}{{n. 饥荒；严重的缺乏；饥饿；奇缺；灾荒}}{{The famine killed millions of people.}}
{{fancy}}{{/ˈfænsi}}{{adj./v./n. 精致的；想象；爱好；花式的；别致的}}{{She has a fancy for collecting rare stamps.}}
{{fatal}}{{/ˈfeɪtl}}{{adj. 致命的；灾难性的；毁灭性的；重大的；命运的}}{{The car accident was fatal to the driver.}}
{{feasible}}{{/ˈfiːzəbl}}{{adj. 可行的；可能的；合理的；可实行的；可用的}}{{The plan is feasible within the given budget.}}
{{feature}}{{/ˈfiːtʃər}}{{n./v. 特征；以…为特色；容貌；特写；专题}}{{The phone has many new features.}}
{{federal}}{{/ˈfedərəl}}{{adj. 联邦的；联邦政府的；联邦制的；同盟的；联合的}}{{The federal government passed a new tax law.}}
{{feedback}}{{/ˈfiːdbæk}}{{n. 反馈；回馈；反应；回复；反馈信息}}{{We welcome feedback from our customers.}}
{{fierce}}{{/fɪəs}}{{adj. 猛烈的；凶猛的；激烈的；狂热的；强烈的}}{{The competition for the job is fierce.}}
{{finance}}{{/ˈfaɪnæns}}{{n./v. 财政；资助；金融；理财；为…提供资金}}{{The government needs to improve its finance management.}}
{{finite}}{{/ˈfaɪnaɪt}}{{adj. 有限的；限定的；有限的；有穷的；限定的}}{{The earth's resources are finite.}}
{{firm}}{{/fɜːm}}{{adj./n. 坚定的；公司；坚固的；稳固的；坚决的}}{{She works for a law firm in the city center.}}
{{fiscal}}{{/ˈfɪskl}}{{adj. 财政的；国库的；会计的； fiscal year；财务的}}{{The government introduced new fiscal policies.}}
{{flaw}}{{/flɔː}}{{n. 缺点；裂纹；瑕疵；缺陷；漏洞}}{{The plan has a serious flaw.}}
{{flee}}{{/fliː}}{{v. 逃跑；逃避；消失；逃离；避开}}{{The refugees fled their homeland to escape the war.}}
{{flexible}}{{/ˈfleksəbl}}{{adj. 灵活的；可变通的；柔韧的；有弹性的；可弯曲的}}{{The company offers flexible working hours.}}
{{flourish}}{{/ˈflʌrɪʃ}}{{v. 繁荣；茂盛；兴旺；挥舞；盛行}}{{The business has flourished under new management.}}
{{fluctuate}}{{/ˈflʌktʃueɪt}}{{v. 波动；涨落；动摇；变动；起伏不定}}{{Stock prices fluctuate daily.}}
{{focus}}{{/ˈfəʊkəs}}{{v./n. 集中；焦点；关注点；聚焦；中心}}{{Please focus on the main points of the lecture.}}
{{forecast}}{{/ˈfɔːkɑːst}}{{v./n. 预测；预报；预示；预想；预见}}{{The weather forecast predicts rain tomorrow.}}
{{forge}}{{/fɔːdʒ}}{{v. 锻造；伪造；建立；缔造；稳步前进}}{{The two countries forged a strong alliance.}}
{{formal}}{{/ˈfɔːml}}{{adj. 正式的；正规的；合乎礼仪的；形式上的；规范的}}{{The invitation requires formal attire.}}
{{format}}{{/ˈfɔːmæt}}{{n./v. 格式；格式化；版式；开本；设计}}{{The report should be in PDF format.}}
{{formula}}{{/ˈfɔːmjələ}}{{n. 公式；方案；配方；准则；客套话}}{{The mathematical formula is used to calculate the area.}}
{{formulate}}{{/ˈfɔːmjuleɪt}}{{v. 制定；明确表达；用公式表示；规划；构想}}{{The government formulated a new economic policy.}}
{{forthcoming}}{{/ˌfɔːθˈkʌmɪng}}{{adj. 即将来临的；乐于助人的； forthcoming； forthcoming； forthcoming}}{{The details of the plan will be available in the forthcoming report.}}
{{fossil}}{{/ˈfɒsl}}{{n. 化石；老顽固；过时的事物；化石的；矿物的}}{{Scientists discovered a rare fossil in the desert.}}
{{foster}}{{/ˈfɒstər}}{{v. 培养；促进；收养；抚育；助长}}{{The program fosters creativity in young students.}}
{{foundation}}{{/faʊnˈdeɪʃn}}{{n. 基础；基金会；地基；创立；根据}}{{Education is the foundation of a successful career.}}
{{fraction}}{{/ˈfrækʃn}}{{n. 分数；小部分；片段；一点儿；少量}}{{Only a fraction of the students passed the exam.}}
{{fragment}}{{/ˈfræɡmənt}}{{n. 碎片；片段；未完成部分；碎块；断片}}{{Fragments of the broken vase were scattered on the floor.}}
{{framework}}{{/ˈfreɪmwɜːk}}{{n. 框架；结构；体系；构架；参照标准}}{{The government established a new legal framework.}}
{{frank}}{{/fræŋk}}{{adj. 坦率的；真诚的；直言不讳的；明显的；免费邮寄的}}{{To be frank, I don't think the plan will work.}}
{{fraud}}{{/frɔːd}}{{n. 欺诈；骗子；冒牌货；骗局；诡计}}{{He was convicted of financial fraud.}}
{{frequent}}{{/ˈfriːkwənt}}{{adj. 频繁的；经常的；常见的；惯常的；屡次的}}{{Frequent exercise helps maintain good health.}}
{{friction}}{{/ˈfrɪkʃn}}{{n. 摩擦；冲突；摩擦力；不和；争执}}{{There is some friction between the two departments.}}
{{frontier}}{{/ˈfrʌntɪər}}{{n. 边界；前沿；新领域；国境；边疆}}{{Space is the final frontier for human exploration.}}
{{frustrate}}{{/frʌˈstreɪt}}{{v. 使沮丧；挫败；阻止；使受挫折；使无效}}{{The lack of progress frustrated the team.}}
{{fulfil/fulfill}}{{/fʊlˈfɪl}}{{v. 履行；实现；满足；执行；达到}}{{She fulfilled her dream of becoming a doctor.}}
{{function}}{{/ˈfʌŋkʃn}}{{n./v. 功能；运转；起作用；职责；函数}}{{The main function of the heart is to pump blood.}}
{{fund}}{{/fʌnd}}{{n./v. 基金；资助；专款；储备；为…提供资金}}{{The university received a large fund for research.}}
{{fundamental}}{{/ˌfʌndəˈmentl}}{{adj. 基本的；根本的；基础的； essential；至关重要的}}{{Freedom of speech is a fundamental human right.}}
{{furnish}}{{/ˈfɜːnɪsh}}{{v. 提供；布置家具；装备；供应；陈设}}{{The apartment is fully furnished.}}
{{furthermore}}{{/ˌfɜːðəˈmɔːr}}{{adv. 此外；而且；再者； furthermore；况且}}{{Furthermore, the study found no evidence of harm.}}
{{fusion}}{{/ˈfjuːʒn}}{{n. 融合；熔合；核聚变；混合；联合}}{{The restaurant offers a fusion of Asian and European cuisine.}}
